 ## Background
-The methods described in this family are derived from various implementations of volume rendering pipelines, including CUDA-based kernels [S2], OpenGL-based raycasting [S1, unofficial], and specialized mesh-based rendering techniques [S3, unofficial]. The use of staging buffers for volume upload is a common pattern in Vulkan and OpenGL to handle large data transfers efficiently [15388-volume-upload-via-staging-buffer.md]. The ClearView technique represents a specific approach to rendering hexahedral meshes by encoding topology into textures [2475-clearview-unified-buffer-construction.md].
